    "result_text": "All 263 tests pass. Here's a summary of what I changed.\n\n## What changed\n\n**`householdId` is now deterministic and automatic** \u2014 `AssignHouseholdId` (`.../function/owner/AssignHouseholdId.java`) now computes it as the first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)` for every owner that has a postcode, independent of `sharesHousehold`. Owners with no postcode have no household (`householdId` null). The old address-based grouping, back-fill, and the `sharesHousehold` gate were removed.\n\n**`sharesHousehold` now only bypasses the duplicate block.** A new function `EnsureHouseholdUnique` + escalation (`DuplicateHouseholdException` / handler / YAML) rejects with **409** any second owner sharing a computed `householdId`, *unless* the request sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member. Wired into `owners.POST.yml` right after `assignHousehold` and before `ensureIdentityUnique`.\n\n**Everything keying off the household uses the computed id:**\n- Duplicate detection: the new household check plus the existing `identityKey` (`tel|email|householdId`) both now see the deterministic value.\n- Household size: `AssignHouseholdSize` already reads `owner.getHouseholdId()`, so it now counts the correct household.\n\n**Declared members aren't flagged.** `AssignPossibleDuplicate` now returns early (clearing the flag) when `sharesHousehold` is set \u2014 \"a declared member is not a suspected duplicate.\"\n\n**Docs** (`openapi.yml`) updated for `sharesHousehold` and `householdId` to describe the new postcode-keyed, deterministic semantics.\n\n## Tests\n- The provided acceptance test `coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId` passes (same lastName+postcode \u2192 same id, even when created without `sharesHousehold`; different lastName \u2192 different id).\n- Added two V1 controller tests: `createOwnerRejectsHouseholdDuplicate` (409) and `createOwnerAllowsHouseholdDuplicateWhenSharesHousehold` (201 + `possibleDuplicate:false`).\n- Full suite: **263 tests, 0 failures**.\n\nOne interpretation note: the spec's phrase \"the household-size input to the membership level\" \u2014 the membership-level formula in this codebase (and its OpenAPI contract) doesn't actually consume household size; it uses email + namesake count. I read that phrase as describing `householdSize`'s role, and satisfied the requirement by making `householdSize` key off the computed `householdId`. I did **not** alter the membership-level formula, since nothing in the code or tests wires household size into it. Let me know if you intended household size to feed the level directly.",
